2. Is 5 GB Storage Enough for All Anime, Manga, and Series as the List Grows?
Yes. 5 GB is massive for this kind of data.
Here is the exact math of why:
We do NOT store video files (which are 1–2 GB each) or large image files on our database.
Videos are hosted on YouTube, Viki, Crunchyroll, and GagaOOLala.
Posters and covers are served by external image CDNs.
Your database only stores text and URLs (e.g., id: "la-bad-buddy", title: "Bad Buddy", url: "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=...").
How much space does text take?
1 complete title record (Title, synopsis, 5 platforms, 24 episode links) takes about 2 KB (0.002 MB).
500 titles = ~1 MB
500,000 titles = ~1 GB
5 GB of storage can hold over 2,500,000 titles and tens of millions of episode links!
Even if you catalog every BL drama, anime, and manga published over the next 20 years, it will use less than 10% of that 5 GB.
